  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1234 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nA hot and dry forecast will prevail across West Central Texas \nthrough the extended period, as the subtropical ridge dominates \nour weather. The center of the upper ridge will remain northeast\nof the area early this week and eventually centered over the Mid-\nMississippi Valley by mid to late week. Daytime highs through the\nperiod will range from the mid and upper 90s across southern\nsections, to the upper 90s to around 102 degrees from the Concho\nValley north into the Big Country. Overnight lows will remain \nwarm, with lows predominantly in the 70s.\n\nDue to the hot temperatures, drying vegetation and lower \nafternoon humidity values, elevated fire weather conditions will \nremain an issue through at least mid week. Low level moisture will\nincrease just a bit by late week into next weekend. This could \nresult in a few showers and isolated thunderstorms over far \nsoutheast counties Friday through Sunday, but confidence remains \nquite low at this time.",
